{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>In the garden</b>, masculine and feminine, and likewise its plural is גנים / גנות. Those who say that \"to work it and to keep it\" refers back to the ground — how is it possible to work and to guard a large place more than a small one? And after he sinned, he was expelled to work the ground, yet he was already working the ground. Rather, \"to work it\" refers to the garden, from whose fruit he would eat; and after he sinned, he went back to eating the grass of the field, which is bread." "The meaning of לעבדה: to water the garden, ולשמרה — to guard it from all the animals, lest they enter there and defile it. And some say that לעבד thus means to perform his commandments, and the commandment is לא תעבוד (you shall not serve [other gods])."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:54.784810522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}